          "taskStatus": "SUCCESS",
          "status": "SUCCESS",
          "results": [
            {
              "message": "<h2>4. Visualize the shared-entity fraud pattern</h2><p>The final query returns both accounts, the shared entity, and both relationship identifiers so Graph Studio can draw the complete pattern.</p><p><strong>What to look for:</strong> A device, IP address, phone, or email in the middle connects the two account nodes. Repeated shared identifiers can support a coordinated-fraud escalation.</p><p>Click <strong>Run</strong>, inspect the graph, and select a node to review its properties.</p>",
              "type": "HTML"
            }
          ]
        },
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 0,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%sql",
          "",
          "SELECT *",
          "FROM GRAPH_TABLE (",
          "  fraud_network",
          "  MATCH (a IS entity)-[e1 IS related_to]->(shared IS entity)<-[e2 IS related_to]-(b IS entity)",
          "  WHERE a.entity_type = 'account'",
          "    AND b.entity_type = 'account'",
          "    AND a.entity_id < b.entity_id",
          "    AND shared.entity_type IN ('device', 'ip_address', 'phone', 'email')",
          "    AND (a.risk_score >= 70 OR b.risk_score >= 70)",
          "  COLUMNS (",
          "    vertex_id(a) AS account_a_id,",
          "    a.entity_key AS account_a,",
          "",
          "    vertex_id(shared) AS shared_entity_id,",
          "    shared.entity_key AS shared_entity,",
          "    shared.entity_type AS shared_type,",
          "",
          "    vertex_id(b) AS account_b_id,",
          "    b.entity_key AS account_b,",
          "",
          "    edge_id(e1) AS e1_id,",
          "    e1.relationship_type AS e1_type,",
          "    edge_id(e2) AS e2_id,",
          "    e2.relationship_type AS e2_type,",
          "",
          "    a.risk_score AS a_risk,",
          "    b.risk_score AS b_risk,",
          "    (a.risk_score + b.risk_score) AS combined_risk",
          "  )",
          ")",
          "ORDER BY combined_risk DESC, shared_entity",
          "FETCH FIRST 25 ROWS ONLY;"
        ],
